# No registry override needed here any more. Every package this scaffold
# depends on — @museumwnf/viewer-core, @museumwnf/viewer-layout,
# @museumwnf/viewer-i18n and the @museumwnf/<dataset>-data packages — now
# publishes to npmjs (registry.npmjs.org), which is npm's own default
# registry. Previously this file pointed the @metanull scope at
# npm.pkg.github.com (GitHub Packages), where those packages were private and
# needed both a scope override and an auth token to install.
#
# If a future package under this scope still needs GitHub Packages (for
# example a not-yet-migrated data package), add it back scoped narrowly —
# `@museumwnf:registry=...` here would again shadow npmjs for every
# @museumwnf package, not just that one.
